# Line-oriented append-only registries: let git auto-merge concurrent appends by
# taking the union of both sides, instead of producing conflict markers that
# stall parallel branches. Union can leave duplicate or unsorted lines, so the
# canonical form (sorted + deduped) is re-asserted by:
#   script/normalize_public_core_allowlist.py --write
# and enforced in CI by the matching `--check` (see script/proof.sh).
#
# IMPORTANT: only use merge=union for files where a duplicated or reordered line
# is harmless and gets normalized away. Never apply it to JSON or other
# structured files — union corrupts their syntax (see proof-manifest.json, which
# is kept conflict-light by deterministic sorting, not union).
docs/product/public-core-reachability-allowlist.psv merge=union
